\draw (O) -- (A) node[midway,below] {$5\text{ cm}$};
\draw (O) -- (B);
\draw (100:2.5) arc[start angle=100,end angle=360,radius=2.5];
\pic[draw,"$100^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.65cm,angle eccentricity=2.1] {angle=A--O--B};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The angle marked is the **exterior** angle of the sector. Find the area of the sector, correct to $2$ decimal places.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\draw (O) -- (0:2.4) node[midway,below] {$9\text{ m}$};
\draw (O) -- (240:2.4);
\draw (240:2.4) arc[start angle=240,end angle=360,radius=2.4];
\draw (0:0.85) arc[start angle=0,end angle=240,radius=0.85];
\node at (120:1.4) {$240^{\circ}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The angle marked is the **exterior** angle of the sector. Find the area of the sector, correct to $1$ decimal place.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (0:2.4);
\coordinate (B) at (135:2.4);
\draw[dashed,gray] (O) circle (2.4);
\draw (O) -- (A);
\draw (O) -- (B);
\draw (A) arc[start angle=0,end angle=135,radius=2.4];
\pic[draw,"$135^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.6cm,angle eccentricity=2] {angle=A--O--B};
\fill (O) circle (1.6pt);
\draw[dashed] (-2.4,0) -- (-2.4,-2.90);
\draw[dashed] (2.4,0) -- (2.4,-2.90);
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-2.4,-2.90) -- (2.4,-2.90) node[midway,below] {$16\text{ mm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The dashed circle is the circle the sector was cut from, and its diameter is marked. Find the area of the sector, correct to $2$ decimal places.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\draw[dashed,gray] (O) circle (2.4);
\draw (O) -- (2.4,0);
\draw (O) -- (0,2.4);
\draw (2.4,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=90,radius=2.4];
\draw (0.32,0) -- (0.32,0.32) -- (0,0.32);
\fill (O) circle (1.6pt);
\draw[dashed] (-2.4,0) -- (-2.4,-2.90);
\draw[dashed] (2.4,0) -- (2.4,-2.90);
